IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa26-support`

-- coa26-ch2c.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 42, Chapter 2 (Individuals and firms), ss 1223 to 1224B: information
-- (matters to be notified to the Secretary of State and to the competent authority, notification of matters relevant to
-- approved third country competent authorities, the power to call for information), restrictions on disclosure, and the offence
-- of disclosure. Lines 17215-17280 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa26-ch1.l4 (MAYBE BOOLEAN; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, each such
-- branch with a FALSE-kind comment; NOTHING otherwise, each branch with a NOTHING-kind comment). Where a section grants a power
-- limited by its own wording, the case outside the limit is NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)).
-- The "recognised" answers (Schedules 10 and 11, coa30), the third country answers (coa27) and the keel's answer to "the competent
-- authority" are INPUTS.

§§ `Information`

§§§ `s 1223 Matters to be notified to the Secretary of State`

-- src:17217 | (1) The Secretary of State may require a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body—
-- src:17218 | (a) to notify him immediately of the occurrence of such events as he may specify in writing and to give him such information in respect of those events as is so specified;
-- src:17219 | (b) to give him, at such times or in respect of such periods as he may specify in writing, such information as is so specified.
@ref s 1223(1) Power to require notification and information (src:17217-17219)
GIVEN `the body is a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is to notify him immediately of the occurrence of such events as the Secretary of State may specify in writing and to give him such information in respect of those events as is so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is to give him, at such times or in respect of such periods as the Secretary of State may specify in writing, such information as is so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223(1) the Secretary of State may require the body to notify or give information` MEANS
    -- the power reaches only the body named in the subsection and only the two kinds of requirement in paragraphs (a) and (b)
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the body is a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body` AND (`the requirement is to notify him immediately of the occurrence of such events as the Secretary of State may specify in writing and to give him such information in respect of those events as is so specified` OR `the requirement is to give him, at such times or in respect of such periods as the Secretary of State may specify in writing, such information as is so specified`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Secretary of State may require" the body named in subsection (1) to notify or give information as in paragraphs (a) and (b)

-- src:17220 | (2) The notices and information required to be given must be such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part.
@ref s 1223(2) The notices and information must be reasonably required (src:17220)
GIVEN `the notice or information required is such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223(2) the notice or information required is within subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the notice or information required is such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notices and information required to be given must be such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require" (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17221 | (3) The Secretary of State may require information given under this section to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner.
@ref s 1223(3) Form and verification (src:17221)
GIVEN `the information is information given under section 1223` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State requires the information to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223(3) the Secretary of State may require the information to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner` MEANS
    IF `the information is information given under section 1223` AND `the Secretary of State requires the information to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Secretary of State may require information given under this section to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner"

-- src:17222 | (4) Any notice or information required to be given under this section must be given in writing unless the Secretary of State specifies or approves some other manner.
@ref s 1223(4) The notice or information must be in writing (src:17222)
GIVEN `the notice or information is required to be given under section 1223` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State specifies or approves some other manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223(4) the notice or information must be given in writing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the notice or information is required to be given under section 1223` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any notice or information required to be given under this section"
        IF `the Secretary of State specifies or approves some other manner` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given in writing unless the Secretary of State specifies or approves some other manner" (an "unless" once met: decided case by case, see the fork register)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


§§§ `s 1223ZA Matters to be notified to the competent authority`

-- src:17224 | (1) The competent authority may require a recognised supervisory body—
-- src:17225 | (a) to notify the competent authority immediately of the occurrence of such events as the competent authority may specify in writing and to give the competent authority such information in respect of those events as is so specified;
-- src:17226 | (b) to give the competent authority, at such times or in respect of such periods as the competent authority may specify in writing, such information as is so specified.
@ref s 1223ZA(1) Power to require notification and information (src:17224-17226)
GIVEN `the body is a recognised supervisory body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is to notify the competent authority immediately of the occurrence of such events as the competent authority may specify in writing and to give the competent authority such information in respect of those events as is so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is to give the competent authority, at such times or in respect of such periods as the competent authority may specify in writing, such information as is so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223ZA(1) the competent authority may require the body to notify or give information` MEANS
    -- the power reaches only the body named in the subsection and only the two kinds of requirement in paragraphs (a) and (b)
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the body is a recognised supervisory body` AND (`the requirement is to notify the competent authority immediately of the occurrence of such events as the competent authority may specify in writing and to give the competent authority such information in respect of those events as is so specified` OR `the requirement is to give the competent authority, at such times or in respect of such periods as the competent authority may specify in writing, such information as is so specified`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the competent authority may require" the body named in subsection (1) to notify or give information as in paragraphs (a) and (b)

-- src:17227 | (2) The notices and information required to be given must be such as the competent authority may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part, the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation .
@ref s 1223ZA(2) The notices and information must be reasonably required (src:17227)
GIVEN `the notice or information required is such as the competent authority may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223ZA(2) the notice or information required is within subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the notice or information required is such as the competent authority may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notices and information required to be given must be such as the competent authority may reasonably require" (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17228 | (3) The competent authority may require information given under this section to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner.
@ref s 1223ZA(3) Form and verification (src:17228)
GIVEN `the information is information given under section 1223ZA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority requires the information to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223ZA(3) the competent authority may require the information to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner` MEANS
    IF `the information is information given under section 1223ZA` AND `the competent authority requires the information to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the competent authority may require information given under this section to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner"

-- src:17229 | (4) Any notice or information required to be given under this section must be given in writing unless the competent authority specifies or approves some other manner.
@ref s 1223ZA(4) The notice or information must be in writing (src:17229)
GIVEN `the notice or information is required to be given under section 1223ZA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority specifies or approves some other manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223ZA(4) the notice or information must be given in writing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the notice or information is required to be given under section 1223ZA` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any notice or information required to be given under this section"
        IF `the competent authority specifies or approves some other manner` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given in writing unless the competent authority specifies or approves some other manner" (an "unless" once met: decided case by case, see the fork register)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


§§§ `s 1223A Notification of matters relevant to approved third country competent authorities`

-- src:17238 | (3) In this section “ notifiable person ” means a member of the recognised supervisory body in question—
-- src:17239 | (a) who is also a third country auditor that has been approved by an approved third country competent authority; and
-- src:17240 | (b) in respect of whom the approved third country competent authority is not the recognised supervisory body itself.
@ref s 1223A(3) "notifiable person" (src:17238-17240)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the recognised supervisory body in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1239 the person is also a third country auditor that has been approved by an approved third country competent authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the approved third country competent authority is the recognised supervisory body itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223A(3) the person is a notifiable person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a member of the recognised supervisory body in question` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“notifiable person” means a member of the recognised supervisory body in question"
        IF `the approved third country competent authority is the recognised supervisory body itself` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in respect of whom the approved third country competent authority is not the recognised supervisory body itself"
        OTHERWISE `s 1239 the person is also a third country auditor that has been approved by an approved third country competent authority` -- (a): another part's answer (coa27); NOTHING stays NOTHING (NOTHING-kind (points outside the text))

-- src:17232 | (a) if a notifiable person becomes eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, unless the notifiable person is an individual;
@ref s 1223A(1)(a) Notification when a notifiable person becomes eligible (src:17232)
GIVEN `the person is a notifiable person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the notifiable person becomes eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifiable person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223A(1)(a) the recognised supervisory body must notify the Secretary of State that the notifiable person has become eligible` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the notifiable person becomes eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A recognised supervisory body must notify the Secretary of State— (a) if a notifiable person becomes eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: decided case by case, see the fork register)
        IF `the notifiable person is an individual` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the notifiable person is an individual"
        OTHERWISE `the person is a notifiable person`

-- src:17233 | (b) if a notifiable person’s eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is withdrawn;
@ref s 1223A(1)(b) Notification when a notifiable person's eligibility is withdrawn (src:17233)
GIVEN `the person is a notifiable person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the notifiable person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223A(1)(b) the recognised supervisory body must notify the Secretary of State that the notifiable person's eligibility is withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `the notifiable person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is withdrawn`
    THEN `the person is a notifiable person`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A recognised supervisory body must notify the Secretary of State— ... (b) if a notifiable person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is withdrawn" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17234 | (c) of the reasons for any such withdrawal.
@ref s 1223A(1)(c) Notification of the reasons for a withdrawal (src:17234)
GIVEN `the person is a notifiable person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the notifiable person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223A(1)(c) the recognised supervisory body must notify the Secretary of State of the reasons for the withdrawal` MEANS
    IF `the notifiable person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is withdrawn`
    THEN `the person is a notifiable person`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) of the reasons for any such withdrawal" (there is a duty only where there is a withdrawal)

-- src:17235 | (2) A recognised supervisory body must also notify the Secretary of State of any reasonable grounds it has for suspecting that—
-- src:17236 | (a) a person has contravened the law of the United Kingdom, or an equivalent third country or transitional third country, and
-- src:17237 | (b) the act or omission constituting that contravention took place on the territory of an equivalent third country or transitional third country.
@ref s 1223A(2) Notification of grounds for suspecting a contravention (src:17235-17237)
GIVEN `the recognised supervisory body has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a person has contravened the law of the United Kingdom, or an equivalent third country or transitional third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission constituting that contravention took place on the territory of an equivalent third country or transitional third country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1223A(2) the recognised supervisory body must notify the Secretary of State of its grounds for suspecting a contravention` MEANS
    IF     `the recognised supervisory body has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a person has contravened the law of the United Kingdom, or an equivalent third country or transitional third country`
       AND `the act or omission constituting that contravention took place on the territory of an equivalent third country or transitional third country`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A recognised supervisory body must also notify the Secretary of State of any reasonable grounds it has for suspecting that— (a) ... and (b) ..." (a duty whose conditions are unmet: decided case by case, see the fork register)


§§§ `s 1224 The Secretary of State's power to call for information`

-- src:17242 | (1) The Secretary of State may by notice in writing require a person within subsection (2) to give him such information as he may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part.
@ref s 1224(1) Power to call for information by notice (src:17242)
GIVEN `the person is within subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is made by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224(1) the Secretary of State may by notice in writing require the person to give the information` MEANS
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the person is within subsection (2)` AND `the requirement is made by notice in writing` AND `the information is such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Secretary of State may by notice in writing require" the persons named "such information as the Secretary of State may reasonably require"

-- src:17243 | (2) The persons within this subsection are—
-- src:17244 | (a) any recognised supervisory body,
-- src:17245 | (b) any recognised qualifying body, and
-- src:17246 | (c) any person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of this Chapter.
@ref s 1224(2) The persons within subsection (2) (src:17243-17246)
GIVEN `the person is a recognised supervisory body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a recognised qualifying body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224(2) the person is within subsection (2)` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons within this subsection are—" (a list closed by "are", read as the keel reads "are": a lawyer's reading)
    `coa26 support any of the answers` `the limbs`
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS
            LIST `the person is a recognised supervisory body`
               , `the person is a recognised qualifying body`
               , `the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2`

-- src:17247 | (3) The Secretary of State may require that any information which he requires under this section is to be given within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as he may specify.
@ref s 1224(3) Time and verification (src:17247)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State requires the information within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as the Secretary of State specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time specified is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224(3) the Secretary of State may require the information to be given within a reasonable time and verified in a specified manner` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State requires the information within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as the Secretary of State specifies` AND `the time specified is reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as the Secretary of State may specify"


§§§ `s 1224ZA The competent authority's power to call for information`

-- src:17249 | (1) The competent authority may by notice in writing require any recognised supervisory body to give the competent authority such information as it may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part, the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation.
@ref s 1224ZA(1) Power to call for information by notice (src:17249)
GIVEN `the body is a recognised supervisory body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is made by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is such as the competent authority may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224ZA(1) the competent authority may by notice in writing require the person to give the information` MEANS
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the body is a recognised supervisory body` AND `the requirement is made by notice in writing` AND `the information is such as the competent authority may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the competent authority may by notice in writing require" the persons named "such information as the competent authority may reasonably require"

-- src:17250 | (2) The competent authority may require that any information which it requires under this section is to be given within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as it may specify.
@ref s 1224ZA(2) Time and verification (src:17250)
GIVEN `the competent authority requires the information within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as the competent authority specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time specified is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224ZA(2) the competent authority may require the information to be given within a reasonable time and verified in a specified manner` MEANS
    IF `the competent authority requires the information within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as the competent authority specifies` AND `the time specified is reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as the competent authority may specify"


§§§ `s 1224A Restrictions on disclosure`

-- src:17256 | (2) This section applies to—
-- src:17257 | (a) a recognised supervisory body,
-- src:17258 | (b) a recognised qualifying body,
-- src:17259 | (c) the competent authority,
-- src:17260 | (d) the Independent Supervisor,
-- src:17261 | (e) the Secretary of State, and
-- src:17262 | (f) a body designated by the Secretary of State under section 1252 (delegation of the Secretary of State's functions).
@ref s 1224A(2) The bodies to which the section applies (src:17256-17262)
GIVEN `sch 10 recognised supervisory bodies: the body is a recognised supervisory body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 11 recognised professional qualifications: the body is a recognised qualifying body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the body is the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the Independent Supervisor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1252 the body is designated by the Secretary of State under section 1252 (delegation of the Secretary of State's functions)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224A(2) the section applies to the body` MEANS
    -- "This section applies to—" a list of bodies, not closed by "only": a body outside the list is NOTHING (NOTHING-kind (list not closed))
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` (`coa26 support any of the answers` `the six limbs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section applies to— (a) a recognised supervisory body, (b) a recognised qualifying body, (c) the competent authority, (d) the Independent Supervisor, (e) the Secretary of State, and (f) a body designated by the Secretary of State under section 1252"
    WHERE
        `the six limbs` MEANS
            LIST `sch 10 recognised supervisory bodies: the body is a recognised supervisory body`
               , `sch 11 recognised professional qualifications: the body is a recognised qualifying body`
               , JUST `s 1173(1) the body is the competent authority`
               , JUST `the body is the Independent Supervisor`
               , JUST `the body is the Secretary of State`
               , `s 1252 the body is designated by the Secretary of State under section 1252 (delegation of the Secretary of State's functions)`

-- src:17252 | (1) This section applies to information (in whatever form)—
-- src:17253 | (a) relating to the private affairs of an individual, or
-- src:17254 | (b) relating to any particular business,
-- src:17255 | that is provided to a body to which this section applies in connection with the exercise of its functions under this Part sections 522 to 524 (notification to appropriate audit authority of resignation or removal of auditor), the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation
@ref s 1224A(1) The information to which the section applies (src:17252-17255)
GIVEN `the information relates to the private affairs of an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to any particular business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided to a body to which this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided in connection with the exercise of the body's functions under Part 42, sections 522 to 524, the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224A(1) the section applies to the information` MEANS
    IF     (`the information relates to the private affairs of an individual` OR `the information relates to any particular business`)
       AND `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the information is provided to a body to which this section applies`
       AND `the information is provided in connection with the exercise of the body's functions under Part 42, sections 522 to 524, the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to information (in whatever form)— (a) relating to the private affairs of an individual, or (b) relating to any particular business, that is provided to a body to which this section applies in connection with the exercise of its functions" (a scope limit with no "only": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

-- src:17264 | (4) Subsection (3) does not apply to any disclosure of information that—
-- src:17265 | (a) is made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the body of any of its functions,
-- src:17266 | (b) is made to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 11A,
-- src:17267 | (c) is of a description specified in Part 2 of that Schedule, or
-- src:17268 | (d) is made in accordance with Part 3 of that Schedule.
@ref s 1224A(4) Disclosures to which subsection (3) does not apply (src:17264-17268)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the body of any of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 11A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is of a description specified in Part 2 of Schedule 11A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 11A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224A(4) subsection (3) does not apply to the disclosure` MEANS
    IF     `the disclosure is made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the body of any of its functions`
        OR `the disclosure is made to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 11A`
        OR `the information is of a description specified in Part 2 of Schedule 11A`
        OR `the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 11A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text says when subsection (3) does not apply, not that it applies in every other case

-- src:17270 | (6) This section does not prohibit the disclosure of information if the information is or has been available to the public from any other source.
@ref s 1224A(6) Information available to the public (src:17270)
GIVEN `the information is or has been available to the public from any other source` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224A(6) the section does not prohibit the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the information is or has been available to the public from any other source`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not prohibit the disclosure of information if the information is or has been available to the public from any other source"

-- src:17271 | (7) Nothing in this section authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation.
@ref s 1224A(7) Data protection legislation (src:17271)
GIVEN `the disclosure would be made in contravention of the data protection legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224A(7) the section authorises the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure would be made in contravention of the data protection legislation`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence only denies authority for a contravening disclosure

-- src:17263 | (3) No such information may, during the lifetime of the individual or so long as the business continues to be carried on, be disclosed without the consent of that individual or (as the case may be) the person for the time being carrying on that business.
@ref s 1224A(3) The bar on disclosure (src:17263)
GIVEN `subsection (1) applies to the information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual is alive, or the business continues to be carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual, or the person for the time being carrying on that business, consents to the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) applies to the disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (6) applies to the disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224A(3) the information may be disclosed` MEANS
    -- This subsection only ever says "no": JUST FALSE when the bar bites, NOTHING when its own limits are not met
    -- (the lifetime or continuing-business period, the consent, the exceptions in subsections (4) and (6)).
    BRANCH
        IF `the individual, or the person for the time being carrying on that business, consents to the disclosure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of that individual or (as the case may be) the person for the time being carrying on that business"
        IF NOT `the individual is alive, or the business continues to be carried on` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during the lifetime of the individual or so long as the business continues to be carried on"
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `subsection (4) applies to the disclosure` OR `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `subsection (6) applies to the disclosure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) does not apply to the disclosures in subsection (4), and subsection (6) does not prohibit the disclosure of public information
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `subsection (1) applies to the information` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No such information may, during the lifetime of the individual or so long as the business continues to be carried on, be disclosed without the consent of that individual or (as the case may be) the person for the time being carrying on that business."
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No such information" reaches only information within subsection (1)

§§§ `s 1224B Offence of disclosure in contravention of section 1224A`

-- src:17273 | (1) A person who discloses information in contravention of section 1224A (restrictions on disclosure) is guilty of an offence, unless—
-- src:17274 | (a) he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been provided as mentioned in section 1224A(1), or
-- src:17275 | (b) he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence.
@ref s 1224B(1) The offence (src:17273-17275)
GIVEN `the person discloses information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1224A(3) the information may be disclosed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been provided as mentioned in section 1224A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1224B(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person discloses information` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who discloses information in contravention of section 1224A"
        IF `coa26 support the answer is NOTHING` `s 1224A(3) the information may be disclosed` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the disclosure is in contravention of section 1224A is not known
        IF NOT (`coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` `s 1224A(3) the information may be disclosed`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the disclosure was not "in contravention of section 1224A"
        IF `the person did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been provided as mentioned in section 1224A(1)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless— (a) he did not know, and had no reason to suspect" (an "unless" once met: decided case by case, see the fork register)
        IF `the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless— ... (b) he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:17276 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:17277 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:17278 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:17279 | (i) in Scotland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum, or to both;
-- src:17280 | (ii) in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum, or to both.
@ref s 1224B(2) Penalty (src:17276-17280)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1224B(2) the penalty for an offence under section 1224B` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (`the penalty` (Period WITH `number of units` IS 2, unit IS Years) `a fine without a stated limit`)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (`the penalty` (Period WITH `number of units` IS 12, unit IS Months) (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1))
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (`the penalty` (Period WITH `number of units` IS 3, unit IS Months) (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1))
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (`the penalty` (Period WITH `number of units` IS 3, unit IS Months) (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1))
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text distinguishes summary conviction in Scotland from summary conviction in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, and a place is not stated
    WHERE
        `the penalty` term fine MEANS
            Penalty WITH
                `how convicted` IS `how the person is convicted`
                `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST term
                `fine not exceeding` IS JUST fine
                `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE -- "or both"

